<title>SWITZERLAND: SMH-Daimler car venture names CEO.</title>
<headline>SMH-Daimler car venture names CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BIEL, Switzerland 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Micro Compact Car AG, the Swiss-German joint venture formed by watchmaker Suisse Microelectronique et d'Horlogerie (SMH) and German automaker Daimler Benz, has named Lars Brorsen as chief executive officer, according to a press statement.</p>
<p>Brorsen, currently vice president and managing director of TRW Occupant Restraint Systems GmbH in Alfdorf, Germany, will join the car concern in January 1997.</p>
<p>The venture, which was formed to produce &quot;Smart&quot; cars, plans to begin production of its micro compact vehicles in autumn 1997, and will begin offering them to customers beginning in spring 1998.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
